1
00:00:00,530 --> 00:00:01,600
23 people…

2
00:00:01,600 --> 00:00:04,520
called Kabir 'bro'.
He lost his job…

3
00:00:04,520 --> 00:00:06,645
Replies? Zero.

4
00:00:06,985 --> 00:00:10,219
In bad times… where
do friends disappear?

5
00:00:10,219 --> 00:00:11,759
In the Bhagavata Purana…

6
00:00:11,759 --> 00:00:14,699
Gajendra, king of
elephants. A crocodile…

7
00:00:14,699 --> 00:00:16,383
seized his leg.

8
00:00:16,383 --> 00:00:19,050
His whole herd came…
but couldn't free him.

9
00:00:19,050 --> 00:00:20,420
Kabir's friends…

10
00:00:20,420 --> 00:00:22,280
maybe aren't bad. They just…

11
00:00:22,280 --> 00:00:23,490
can't help.

12
00:00:23,490 --> 00:00:26,857
He fought for a thousand years…
yet blamed no one.

13
00:00:26,967 --> 00:00:30,137
"My own kin cannot free me…

14
00:00:30,137 --> 00:00:33,685
I go to Him, the highest refuge."

15
00:00:34,295 --> 00:00:35,485
My own…

16
00:00:35,485 --> 00:00:38,815
can't free me. I
go to His shelter…

17
00:00:38,815 --> 00:00:40,477
the refuge of all.

18
00:00:40,477 --> 00:00:42,097
Kabir muted the group…

19
00:00:42,097 --> 00:00:44,220
then made one call… to Papa.

20
00:00:44,470 --> 00:00:47,429
"Papa… I lost my job."—
"Come home, beta."

21
00:00:47,549 --> 00:00:48,919
In your bad times…

22
00:00:48,919 --> 00:00:51,977
who showed up? The group…
or just one person?
